00:00:07.420 --> 00:00:09.540
What up Wisecrack, Greg here.

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:11.380
Have you been hustling lately?

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:12.870
It seems like everybody is.

00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:15.410
Whether you're busting your
balls at the nine-to-five,

00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:17.270
or adding an Uber shift at night,

00:00:17.270 --> 00:00:21.230
or selling your knitted frogs
on Etsy: the hustle is real.

00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:23.120
The culture surrounding hustling

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:25.930
means that rest is our last priority.

00:00:25.930 --> 00:00:28.920
Hustle culture encourages
us to spend our free time

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:31.520
pursuing money, and economic stability,

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:33.360
by any means necessary.

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:35.650
It's the embodiment of
the classic philosophy

00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:39.200
of pulling oneself up by the
bootstraps to make ends meet,

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:41.730
especially in today's
tough economic climate.

00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:43.850
But, ironically, the term "bootstrapping",

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:46.470
coined in the 1800s,
was initially intended

00:00:46.470 --> 00:00:49.400
to reference something
being literally impossible.

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:52.040
Impossible like, pulling
yourself over a fence

00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:53.680
by the straps of your boots.

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:56.870
Or crossing a river by
the straps of your boots.

00:00:56.870 --> 00:01:00.520
Or flying to the moon by
the straps of your boots.

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:03.350
Yet today, the phrase basically means

00:01:03.350 --> 00:01:05.960
you can overcome all barriers to success

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:08.410
through sheer determination and hard work.

00:01:08.410 --> 00:01:11.580
The bootstraps narrative
tells us that no matter what,

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:15.340
if we work hard enough, we
will eventually be successful,

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:17.660
just like those self-made millionaires

00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:19.977
who struck gold with just a small,

00:01:19.977 --> 00:01:22.890
$1 million loan from their parents.

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:24.610
And hustle culture success stories

00:01:24.610 --> 00:01:27.680
are endlessly parroted by the mass media.

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:30.730
Often, these success stories
come from celebrities

00:01:30.730 --> 00:01:35.710
using existing social media
clout to, say, push diet teas,

00:01:35.710 --> 00:01:38.650
perfumes, or even stoner pottery.

00:01:38.650 --> 00:01:40.720
And while it may have worked for Rihanna,

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:43.650
most of us are in a more hopeless place.

00:01:43.650 --> 00:01:45.520
So, today we're gonna ask:

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:48.440
is hustle culture a
positive motivational force,

00:01:48.440 --> 00:01:51.450
or is it just a buzzword
used to make us feel bad

00:01:51.450 --> 00:01:53.487
for using our free time to relax?

00:01:53.487 --> 00:01:55.320
- [Princess Carolyn]
Starting now, you are a hard,

00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:56.470
heartless career gal.

00:01:56.470 --> 00:01:58.160
